// An operator where an expression belongs.
//
// The atom parser's last resort is "whatever text is here is a name", which
// for an operator token manufactures a variable called `/` -- and the first
// complaint anyone sees is the access pass reporting an undefined variable
// with a punctuation mark for a name, three times, for one mistake. An
// operator is never a name, so it is reported here, once, as what it is.

no_op_atom(int[] pos) {
  if(cur_kind(pos) == "op") {
    syn_err(pos, unexpected_msg(cur_text(pos)));
  }
} return void;

// The lexer folds a whole `/* ... */` into one `/*` token precisely so this
// can say what the mistake actually was.
unexpected_msg(string t) {
  string s = "unexpected token '" + t + "'";
  if(t == "/*") {
    s = "block comments are not supported; use // for a line comment";
  }
} return string s;
